Frontend: HTML, CSS and JavaScript interface for searching books by title, author, or ISBN, and scanning books by ISBN-13. Includes a "Get Token" button following Wayne's standalone dev harness pattern, a tabbed layout covering My Books, Search/Scan, and Reader Profile, and inline form handling for adding and updating reading records.

API (C#): ASP.NET Core Minimal API following Wayne's EDP single-file pattern (Program.cs only, no middleware or repository layers). Endpoints include:

POST /api/ral/v01/books/search — searches books by title, author, or ISBN using ral.ral_SearchBooks_JSON
POST /api/ral/v01/books/scan — submits an ISBN-13 and returns matching books using ral.ral_ScanBook_JSON
POST /api/ral/v01/user-books — adds or upserts a reading record using ral.ral_AddBookRead_JSON
PUT /api/ral/v01/user-books/{userBookId} — updates a reading record using ral.ral_UpdateBookRead_JSON
GET /api/ral/v01/user-books — retrieves the current member's reading list using ral.ral_UserBooks_CRUD_JSON
DELETE /api/ral/v01/user-books/{userBookId} — soft-deactivates a reading record using ral.ral_UserBooks_CRUD_JSON
JWT authentication is validated inline using JsonWebTokenHandler with a symmetric signing key. SESSION_CONTEXT TenantID and MemberID are set on every SQL connection from the verified JWT claims. All SQL access is through Wayne's stored procedures only — no direct table access.

Database: Integration with SQL Server tables ral.ral_UserBooks, ral.ral_Books, ral.ral_BookAuthors, and ral.ral_BookLookupLog (via stored procedures only).

Stored Procedures:

ral.ral_SearchBooks_JSON — searches books across title, author, or ISBN fields and logs every lookup to ral_BookLookupLog with a result status (MATCHED, MULTIPLE_MATCHES, NOT_MATCHED)
ral.ral_ScanBook_JSON — accepts an ISBN-13 or ISBN-10 scan and delegates to ral_SearchBooks_JSON with SearchType = ISBN_SCAN
ral.ral_AddBookRead_JSON — upserts a reading record; auto-creates the book and author records in ral_Books and ral_Authors if they do not already exist
ral.ral_UpdateBookRead_JSON — updates an existing reading record's status, rating, review text, and dates (delegates to ral_UserBooks_CRUD_JSON UPDATE)
ral.ral_UserBooks_CRUD_JSON — used for SELECT (retrieve member reading list) and DELETE (soft-deactivate a reading record)
